$\sin x$ and $\cos x$ intersects each other at $\left(\frac{\pi}{4}, \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\right) \begin{aligned}
\therefore\text{ Required area }&=\int_{0}^{\pi/ 4} \cos x d x-\int_{0}^{\pi/ 4} \sin x d x \\
&=[\sin x]_{0}^{\pi/ 4}-[-\cos x]_{0}^{\pi/ 4} \\
&=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}-\left[\frac{-1}{\sqrt{2}}+1\right]=\frac{2}{\sqrt{2}}-1=\sqrt{2}-1
\end{aligned}
$
